content:
If Jane is not guilty, it is **fairly likely** that at least some of the injuries later identified on Ben were not apparent, not yet detectable, or not actually present in a clinically observable way when he arrived at the hospital.

Reasons:
- some findings are only discovered on autopsy or specialized examination;
- some injuries are subtle and may be missed in emergency treatment;
- in a resuscitation setting, nurses are focused on saving life rather than documenting every possible injury;
- some apparent injuries may reflect post-mortem change, artefact, or interpretation after the fact.

So under the not-guilty hypothesis, the fact that nurses did not note the injuries does not seem especially surprising.

